.SS "\fBAnimatedAttributes\fP setTransform (array number matrix)"

.PP
Replace the affine transform immediately\&. Unlike \fBtransform()\fP, replaces the matrix instead of postmultiplying it\&. \fBAnimatedAttributes\fP preserves its logical width and height, updates its shared \fBAnimated\fP transform components, and cancels conflicting transform animation\&. It rejects nonfinite or non-affine matrices and nonzero matrix columns whose corresponding logical dimension is zero\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fImatrix\fP Array of nine numbers in column-major order\&. For a 2D affine transform use [a, b, 0, c, d, 0, tx, ty, 1], mapping (x,y) to (a*x+c*y+tx, b*x+d*y+ty)\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
This object, for chaining\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBExample\fP
.RS 4

.PP
.nf
style\&.setTransform([1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 20, 10, 1]);

.fi
.PP
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBtransform()\fP, \fBgetTransform()\fP 
.RE
.PP

